  "problem": "Insert the missing number in the multiplication problem below.\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>\n<table align=\"center\" width=\"100\" height=\"100\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"3\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\" align=\"center\">$\\times $</td>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\" align=\"center\">$=$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td>\n\n<table align=\"center\" width=\"100\" height=\"100\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
  "worked_solution": "We have $\\frac{2}{6}$ on the left and $\\frac{6}{24}$ on the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130839/assets/918db9e617e1830739d91a5799f7862a56f988f9b5dc6ead60f1cdc41d332867.png)\n\nThe shape on the right-hand side is split into $4$ equal parts by horizontal lines.\nSo, the shaded part on the right is $\\frac{3}{4}$ of the shaded part on the left. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{6}\\times \\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{6}{24}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $3.$",
